WEBVTT

00:00:00.469 --> 00:00:05.165
Welcome to Alaventra. Rank in
search. Get recommended by AI.

00:00:06.143 --> 00:00:10.818
In tutorial 3.4, you'll turn a
client result into a case study,

00:00:10.868 --> 00:00:14.210
with its own page and proof
your other pages can cite.

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:19.610
First, open Run an analysis, and
find Write a case study under Create.

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:20.647
Click Start.

00:00:23.244 --> 00:00:28.059
Next, describe the client. If you can't
name them, type a short description,

00:00:28.109 --> 00:00:30.651
and switch off We may
name the client publicly.

00:00:32.698 --> 00:00:37.522
Add their industry and location, and the
country your case study page should target.

00:00:39.694 --> 00:00:44.119
Then add the service you delivered, the
challenge before you came in, what you did,

00:00:44.169 --> 00:00:45.439
and how long it took.

00:00:49.219 --> 00:00:52.919
Now add the results, with
numbers the client would confirm.

00:00:52.969 --> 00:00:56.159
A short client quote, and who
said it, makes it stronger.

00:00:58.694 --> 00:01:02.569
Type the search you want the page
to be found for, or leave it empty,

00:01:02.619 --> 00:01:04.183
and one is chosen for you.

00:01:06.690 --> 00:01:10.215
The summary shows the credits
it uses and the time it takes.

00:01:10.265 --> 00:01:12.778
When you're ready, click
Write the case study.

00:01:15.190 --> 00:01:17.645
When it's written, about 15 minutes later,

00:01:17.695 --> 00:01:22.645
your case study joins the proof library
on the Content page, with its own page,

00:01:22.695 --> 00:01:27.433
and later pages cite it. You can also
start one here with Write a case study.

00:01:28.453 --> 00:01:32.963
So, open Write a case study, describe
the client, describe the project,

00:01:33.013 --> 00:01:36.552
add the results, choose the
keyword, and write the case study.

00:01:37.527 --> 00:01:43.358
Your proof library is growing. Next,
run your first analysis in tutorial 4.1.
